{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E5r3p2wDuQQqnYKFqaA9Kq","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Gap hunt: E10 — Audit across service boundaries\n2\t\n3\tA reviewer couldn't decide whether this item is met. **Your job is to find out whether any\n4\tcheck below is false in this codebase.** The reviewer's partial answers and the code they\n5\tlooked at are shown. Read the code, and open the repo files the checks point to.\n6\t\n7\tFor each check, decide:\n8\t- **fails**: you found the line that makes it false (a missing control, a bypass, a\n9\t  value never used, an exception that continues, a filter that lets something through).\n10\t  Quote that line;\n11\t- **holds**: you found the code that makes it true in every case;\n12\t- **unclear**: you can't tell from this repo.\n13\t\n14\t**The requirement for E10:** Rebuild a run across the gateway, tool services, and delegated workers, with all six identity fields kept. Check that the agent can't erase or rewrite its audit history, either directly or by asking a more powerful tool or peer. Check that a vendor boundary doesn't leave any action untraceable to the agent and instance that did it.\n15\t\n16\tIf a check fails, also copy the words from this requirement that the code breaks into\n17\t`violates`. Then write your answer (format at the end).\n18\t\n19\t\n20\t## E10.1\n21\t\n22\t**Check:** The gateway, tool services, and delegated workers each write audit records with all six identity fields and the shared trace context.\n23\t\n24\t**How to verify:** 1) Find audit writers in the gateway, tool services, and delegated workers. 2) Check each writes all six identity fields and the shared trace context. 3) Answer no if any component writes records without them or starts a new trace. Answer unknown if a component's code is outside this repo.\n25\t\n26\t**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n27\t\n28\t**Reviewer's note:** Gateway and tool service audit records are outside the repo; only the agent and extractor write audit rows\n29\t\n30\t(no evidence cited)\n31\t\n32\t## E10.2\n33\t\n34\t**Check:** The agent's credentials have no permission to delete, update, or overwrite audit records (for example an append-only or WORM store with IAM denies).\n35\t\n36\t**How to verify:** 1) Find the agent's IAM role or database grants and the audit store config. 2) Check the agent has no delete, update, or overwrite rights (`DeleteObject`, overwriting `PutObject`, `UPDATE`, `DELETE`, `TRUNCATE`) and the store is append-only or WORM (Object Lock). 3) Answer no if the agent's credentials can delete or rewrite records, or grant `*`. Answer unknown if these are set outside this repo.\n37\t\n38\t**Reviewer's evidence:** migrations/001_init.sql:121 — \"GRANT SELECT, INSERT ON audit_events TO procurement_agent;\"\n39\t\n40\t**Reviewer's note:** The agent role can only insert and read audit rows\n41\t\n42\t`migrations/001_init.sql` lines 109–133 (cited lines marked >):\n43\t```\n44\t 109  );\n45\t 110  \n46\t 111  CREATE TABLE run_start_window (\n47\t 112      scope   text NOT NULL,\n48\t 113      key     text NOT NULL,\n49\t 114      minute  timestamptz NOT NULL,\n50\t 115      starts  integer NOT NULL,\n51\t 116      PRIMARY KEY (scope, key, minute)\n52\t 117  );\n53\t 118  \n54\t 119  -- Runtime role: append-only audit, no access to control flags beyond reading.\n55\t 120  REVOKE ALL ON ALL TABLES IN SCHEMA public FROM procurement_agent;\n56\t 121> GRANT SELECT, INSERT ON audit_events TO procurement_agent;\n57\t 122  GRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE ON approvals TO procurement_agent;\n58\t 123  GRANT SELECT ON approvers TO procurement_agent;\n59\t 124  GRANT SELECT, INSERT ON documents TO procurement_agent;\n60\t 125  GRANT SELECT, INSERT ON dept_notes TO procurement_agent;\n61\t 126  GRANT SELECT ON control_flags TO procurement_agent;\n62\t 127  GRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE ON spend_quota TO procurement_agent;\n63\t 128  GRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE ON run_start_window TO procurement_agent;\n64\t 129  \n65\t 130  -- Operators: halt and resume.\n66\t 131  GRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE ON control_flags TO procurement_ops;\n67\t 132  GRANT SELECT ON audit_events TO procurement_ops;\n68\t 133  GRANT SELECT, UPDATE (verified, verified_by, quarantined) ON dept_notes TO procurement_ops;\n69\t```\n70\t\n71\t## E10.3\n72\t\n73\t**Check:** No tool or peer the agent can call is able to delete or rewrite audit records on its behalf, or such requests are held for approval under B05.\n74\t\n75\t**How to verify:** 1) List the tools and peers the agent can call. 2) For each, check whether it can delete or rewrite audit records (database admin, log management, storage tools). 3) Answer no if any can and such requests are not held for approval under B05.\n76\t\n77\t**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n78\t\n79\t**Reviewer's note:** Whether any ERP operation can alter audit records on the agent's behalf is outside this repo\n80\t\n81\t(no evidence cited)\n82\t\n83\t## E10.4\n84\t\n85\t**Check:** Calls into vendor services are mapped from the gateway's verified identity and correlation ID to the vendor's job or receipt ID.\n86\t\n87\t**How to verify:** 1) Find calls into vendor services. 2) Check the gateway stores its verified identity and correlation ID together with the vendor's job or receipt ID. 3) Answer no if the vendor ID is not stored, or stored without the link to identity and correlation ID.\n88\t\n89\t**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n90\t\n91\t**Reviewer's note:** Vendor-side correlation of payments and ERP calls to run and instance is outside this repo\n92\t\n93\t(no evidence cited)\n94\t\n95\t## Your answer\n96\t\n97\tWrite this JSON to E10.verdict.json in this folder (or put it in verdicts.json under \"E10\"):\n98\t```json\n99\t{\"verdict\": \"upheld | failed | unclear\",\n100\t \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"E10.1\", \"result\": \"holds | fails | unclear\", \"evidence\": \"path:line\", \"quote\": \"exact code\", \"note\": \"why\"}],\n101\t \"not